# Every repository the Brokered Composition builds from: the folder under
# apps/, then the remote.
#
# One list and two readers. `checkout-apps.sh` clones each repository at its
# `federation` branch; `check-federation-drift.sh` asks GitHub how far that
# branch has fallen behind the repository's own default branch. Written out
# twice, the two would disagree the day a sixth application is integrated, and
# the one that disagreed silently would be the check.
#
# The folder is named after the repository rather than after the application,
# because what lands in it is that repository and `git` is run in it by hand
# afterwards.
#
# compose.apps.yaml builds from these paths, and the two lists have to agree: a
# repository added here without a service there is a slow clone nobody uses.
#
# A reader skips a line that opens with `#` and a line that is empty. Nothing
# else is a comment: the second field is a URL, and `#` inside one is part of
# it.
gdalface|https://github.com/Ibercivis/gdalface.git
citsci-api|https://github.com/Ibercivis/citsci-api.git
geonity|https://github.com/Ibercivis/Geonity.git
openred|https://github.com/Ibercivis/OpenRed.git
openred-react|https://github.com/Ibercivis/openred-react.git
